    "updated_at": "2021-10-25T15:32:02Z",
    "body": "Is there any precedence for this? The AWS module prints the expiration time, but it just reads the expiration time from local sources. `vault token lookup` makes an API call to the Vault server. Probably what Starship should do is make the API call itself (spawning processes can expensive on Windows), and cache the expiration time somehow using the hash of the token so it can avoid making API calls every time the prompt needs to be rendered.",
